{{-- Auth chrome. Layout group 'auth'.

    A FRAGMENT, not a document -- same contract as marketing.stx. stx synthesises
    <!DOCTYPE>, <html lang>, <head> and <body> from config/ui.ts app.head merged with
    each page's head. Writing a doctype or an html tag here, even inside a comment
    (the test is an unanchored regex over the rendered string), makes hasDocumentShell()
    true and every page's title and description is dropped. Never add one.

    Replaces the hand-written `<meta name="stx-layout" content="auth">` that login,
    register and sites/new each carried. That meta was a hint the pages asserted about
    themselves; the FILENAME is what actually names a layout group, so the two could
    disagree and nothing would say so.

    The <style> block below was copy-pasted, byte for byte, into login.stx and
    register.stx, and into sites/new.stx minus the five .oauth-btn/.divider rules it
    does not use. Those five are harmless there -- no element carries the class -- and
    one shared block beats three that drift.

    <main> lives HERE and pages must not declare their own: fragment extraction slices
    from the first <main> to the LAST </main>, so a second one makes the router swap the
    wrong span. Pages yield their own width wrapper instead, because they disagree about
    it -- login and register want max-w-sm, sites/new wants max-w-md. --}}

@head
<style>
/* The marketing palette under this layout's token names, so signing in looks
  like the site you came from -- dark by default, light when the OS asks or the
  reader picked it (config/ui.ts app.colorMode writes <html data-theme> before
  first paint; the attribute beats the media query either way). */
:root {
  color-scheme: dark;
  --bg: #0a0c0e; --panel: #101317; --border: rgba(233,238,240,0.12);
  --text: #eef2f3; --text-2: #9aa4a9; --text-3: #7b878c;
  --accent: #46d3c0; --accent-ink: #04201c; --danger: #f87171;
  --sans: 'Geist', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; --mono: 'Geist Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
  :root:not([data-theme="dark"]) { color-scheme: light;
    --bg: #fafbfb; --panel: #ffffff; --border: rgba(12,18,20,0.12);
    --text: #0c1214; --text-2: #4e5a5f; --text-3: #66737a;
    --accent: #0f7c72; --accent-ink: #ffffff; --danger: #c93434; }
}
:root[data-theme="light"] { color-scheme: light;
  --bg: #fafbfb; --panel: #ffffff; --border: rgba(12,18,20,0.12);
  --text: #0c1214; --text-2: #4e5a5f; --text-3: #66737a;
  --accent: #0f7c72; --accent-ink: #ffffff; --danger: #c93434; }
body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); font-family: var(--sans); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
.wordmark { font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
.field { background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; color: var(--text); }
.field:focus { outline: none; border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 16%, transparent); }
.btn { background: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink); border-radius: 10px; transition: transform 0.12s ease, opacity 0.15s ease; }
.btn:hover { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 88%, #000); }
.btn:active { transform: translateY(1px); }
.btn:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: default; }
.err { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--danger) 12%, transparent); color: var(--danger); }
.ok { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 12%, transparent); color: var(--accent); }
.oauth-btn { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; color: var(--text); background: var(--panel); transition: border-color 0.15s ease, transform 0.12s ease; }
.oauth-btn:hover { border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 45%, var(--border)); }
.oauth-btn:active { transform: translateY(1px); }
.divider { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-3); font-size: 12px; }
.divider::before, .divider::after { content: ""; height: 1px; flex: 1; background: var(--border); }
</style>
@stack('styles')
@endhead

<main class="flex items-center justify-center px-5 py-12 min-h-[100dvh]">
@yield('content')
</main>

@stack('scripts')
